<!-- NOT LISTED, on purpose:
     insurance.html  The page renders, but everything on it past the login
                     form is auth-gated, so an indexed URL would send a
                     searcher to a sign-in screen and give a crawler an
                     empty shell to rank. It is linked from the portal,
                     which is where its audience arrives from.
     landing.html    Identical to "/" (verified byte-for-byte). Listing both
                     would be a duplicate-content entry pointing at one page.
     portal.html,
     verify.html     Application surfaces, not content.
     /docs/archive/  nginx returns 404 for that prefix. -->
